238
00:15:28,561 --> 00:15:30,621
They were in bed together.

239
00:15:30,797 --> 00:15:32,891
Now, eat.

240
00:15:55,421 --> 00:15:58,414
- Hello, detective.
- Hi. This is Ben Matlock.

241
00:15:58,591 --> 00:16:00,685
He's the lawyer
defending Rick Hamlin.

242
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:03,227
Now, why would you wanna
do a thing like that, Mr. Matlock?

243
00:16:04,530 --> 00:16:06,522
Ooh. Mulberry stains.

244
00:16:06,833 --> 00:16:09,114
You know, you don't get
them off, they'll ruin your paint.

245
00:16:09,502 --> 00:16:12,870
Mr. Matlock here is kind of an
expert when it comes to stains.

246
00:16:13,039 --> 00:16:14,199
Would you mind if we went in?

247
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:16,900
This is going to be rather
painful. I'd like to get it over with.

248
00:16:18,077 --> 00:16:19,443
Thank you.

249
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:23,882
Were you here the night,
uh, Ray was murdered?

250
00:16:24,050 --> 00:16:26,451
We all know you read
my statement, Mr. Matlock.

251
00:16:26,786 --> 00:16:28,516
After you.

252
00:16:32,525 --> 00:16:36,587
It occurred to me this morning
that if I had been in the room,

253
00:16:36,762 --> 00:16:39,163
I would've been killed too.

254
00:16:39,932 --> 00:16:42,128
Uh, my things are in the
closet. May I get them?

255
00:16:42,301 --> 00:16:43,530
Mm.

256
00:16:43,970 --> 00:16:46,530
She dropped the wine
when she saw the body.

257
00:16:46,706 --> 00:16:48,902
- Club soda will get that out, right?
- Mm.

258
00:16:51,944 --> 00:16:54,379
- You pretty good around the house?
- Yeah.

259
00:16:54,547 --> 00:16:55,810
Mm.

260
00:16:55,982 --> 00:16:58,508
- Ooh, iron your own shirts.
- Yeah.

261
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:03,213
- Do, uh, some cooking, little cleaning?
- Yeah.

262
00:17:03,389 --> 00:17:06,257
Me, I'm no good at that stuff.

263
00:17:06,425 --> 00:17:08,860
You're the guy I've
been looking for.

264
00:17:12,899 --> 00:17:15,630
Did you find the bag lady the
neighbor saw leaving the scene?

265
00:17:15,801 --> 00:17:16,962
Oh, bag lady.

266
00:17:17,136 --> 00:17:19,662
Well, Mr. Yates said
he saw a short woman

267
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:22,035
in a red sweatshirt
and yellow scarf.

268
00:17:22,208 --> 00:17:24,336
Not exactly what I'd call
a detailed description.

269
00:17:24,510 --> 00:17:27,480
You're not even gonna look for
her? She might have seen the killer.

270
00:17:27,647 --> 00:17:29,843
Oh, Mr. Matlock, news flash.

271
00:17:30,016 --> 00:17:32,713
- I already got the killer.
- Mm.

272
00:17:33,152 --> 00:17:35,815
Uh, excuse me. Did, uh...?

273
00:17:35,988 --> 00:17:38,389
Ahem. Did you see her?

274
00:17:38,558 --> 00:17:41,027
- Did I see who?
- The bag lady.

275
00:17:41,193 --> 00:17:46,359
Oh, no. I, to be quite honest, never
give people like that a second glance.

276
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:49,091
What do you do?

277
00:17:49,669 --> 00:17:52,571
- What do you mean, what do I do?
- I mean, work.

278
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:54,172
I edit a weekly magazine.

279
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:56,707
Huh. Is it hard?

280
00:17:56,976 --> 00:17:59,844
No. It's time-consuming.

281
00:18:00,012 --> 00:18:03,710
Mondays and Tuesdays I
normally work till midnight.

282
00:18:03,883 --> 00:18:06,148
But Wednesdays, after
we go to press, I celebrate.

283
00:18:06,452 --> 00:18:08,978
That's the time that I
would spend with Ray.

284
00:18:09,155 --> 00:18:10,646
That became our night.

285
00:18:12,058 --> 00:18:14,721
I would spend
Wednesdays with Ray.

286
00:18:14,894 --> 00:18:17,193
I thought about it all week,

287
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:19,823
just being with him.

288
00:18:23,502 --> 00:18:26,734
- May I go, please?
- Yeah, yeah.

289
00:18:29,609 --> 00:18:31,771
Nice-looking dame.

290
00:18:31,944 --> 00:18:34,004
She's okay.

291
00:18:35,481 --> 00:18:39,350
Did you ever hear of a
nightclub called Martell's?

292
00:18:39,518 --> 00:18:41,350
Yeah, it's a trendy
place, anything goes.

293
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:42,988
- Yeah.
- You know.

294
00:18:43,155 --> 00:18:46,523
Look at all these
credit-card charges here.

295
00:18:46,692 --> 00:18:49,753
Ray, looks like he went
there Monday and Tuesdays.

296
00:18:49,929 --> 00:18:52,899
Ho! When the cat's away...

297
00:18:53,065 --> 00:18:56,160
- You know where it is?
- Sure. It's, uh, 19th and Adams. Why?

298
00:19:25,498 --> 00:19:27,967
Look for a spot without
people in it and go.

299
00:19:28,134 --> 00:19:29,864
- I hear you.
- Move along.

300
00:19:30,036 --> 00:19:32,403
- Hey, what up, guys?
- What's up?

301
00:19:35,541 --> 00:19:37,567
Well, hi, Sailor.

302
00:19:38,711 --> 00:19:40,475
Hi.

303
00:19:46,752 --> 00:19:50,120
Did you see that
wild-looking girl?

304
00:19:50,289 --> 00:19:53,316
Who, her? She's a he.

305
00:20:02,101 --> 00:20:03,865
- How you doing?
- Okay, I guess.

306
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:05,095
All right.

307
00:20:05,671 --> 00:20:09,972
- Hey. Wow, man. Outstanding suit.
- Thanks.

308
00:20:10,142 --> 00:20:11,940
Oh, Tim, this is Ben. Ben, Tim.

309
00:20:12,111 --> 00:20:13,977
- Oh, hi.
- You wanna dance?

310
00:20:15,448 --> 00:20:17,178
- What?
- You wanna dance?

311
00:20:19,318 --> 00:20:20,616
- With you?
- Yeah.

312
00:20:20,786 --> 00:20:22,482
No.

313
00:20:38,204 --> 00:20:41,197
What's the matter, you
didn't like Tim? He liked you.

314
00:20:41,507 --> 00:20:44,568
- What kind of place is this?
- I think you hurt his feelings.

315
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:46,440
He'll just have to get over it.

316
00:20:47,046 --> 00:20:48,571
Heartbreaker.

317
00:20:48,748 --> 00:20:49,807
Hey, Bobby.

318
00:20:50,116 --> 00:20:53,177
Hey, Pat. What
can I get for you?

319
00:20:53,352 --> 00:20:55,412
Nothing she can spill.

320
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:57,489
Not a thing. I gotta go.

321
00:20:57,656 --> 00:21:01,559
But, look, this dude here wants
to ask you a couple of questions.

322
00:21:01,727 --> 00:21:04,754
Do me a favor.
Tell him the truth.

323
00:21:06,432 --> 00:21:07,866
What?

324
00:21:08,701 --> 00:21:10,169
Uh...

325
00:21:11,537 --> 00:21:13,529
You know a guy
named Ray Wallace?

326
00:21:13,706 --> 00:21:15,971
You bet. Dude was
famous. Came in here a lot.

327
00:21:16,142 --> 00:21:18,407
He come in by himself
or was he with a...?

328
00:21:18,577 --> 00:21:21,479
The last couple of weeks,
uh, he was with the same girl.

329
00:21:21,647 --> 00:21:25,311
I know her name.
Dunn, Marsha Dunn.

330
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:13,996
- Hey, Neil.
- Oh, hey, Ben.

331
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:15,395
What's going on?

332
00:22:15,568 --> 00:22:18,197
Some woman either
OD'd or offed herself.

333
00:22:18,370 --> 00:22:21,033
Looks like it happened
sometime yesterday.

334
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:24,274
Her name wasn't
Marsha Dunn, was it?

335
00:22:24,610 --> 00:22:27,478
Yes. How did you know?

336
00:22:27,713 --> 00:22:30,080
I don't know. Just lucky.

337
00:22:57,443 --> 00:22:59,435
I have no idea who
Marsha Dunn is.

338
00:22:59,778 --> 00:23:00,837
Why do you ask, detective?

339
00:23:01,013 --> 00:23:03,448
Because there's a mulberry
tree outside of her apartment.

340
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:05,809
I beg your pardon?

341
00:23:05,985 --> 00:23:08,750
And you have mulberry
stains on your car.

342
00:23:08,921 --> 00:23:12,517
<i>And she was seeing your
late boyfriend, Ray Wallace.</i>

343
00:23:12,892 --> 00:23:14,326
<i>Really?</i>

344
00:23:14,793 --> 00:23:18,389
<i>And because she was found
dead yesterday. Apparent suicide.</i>

345
00:23:18,564 --> 00:23:23,798
<i>The medical examiner says she
ingested something called Darzac.</i>

346
00:23:24,103 --> 00:23:25,799
<i>How odd.</i>

347
00:23:26,171 --> 00:23:28,367
<i>That's what my father
used when he killed himself.</i>

348
00:23:28,741 --> 00:23:31,609
The day after your stepmother
was found shot to death.

349
00:23:33,412 --> 00:23:35,347
Ancient history.

350
00:23:35,514 --> 00:23:37,194
Is there a point to
all of this, detective?

351
00:23:37,349 --> 00:23:38,442
Point? Oh, no.

352
00:23:38,617 --> 00:23:41,746
Except the people in your
life have a tendency to die.

353
00:23:42,922 --> 00:23:44,788
This magazine you edit,
it's a medical journal?

354
00:23:44,957 --> 00:23:45,981
Yes, it is.

355
00:23:46,425 --> 00:23:50,157
Editing all that scientific
stuff must be pretty difficult.

356
00:23:50,930 --> 00:23:53,456
Not at all. Actually,
it's quite fun.

357
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:55,732
Pretty smart, aren't you?

358
00:23:56,235 --> 00:23:57,396
Yes, I am.

359
00:23:57,703 --> 00:24:00,366
<i>Also pretty possessive
when it comes to men?</i>

360
00:24:00,539 --> 00:24:02,735
<i>I am no more possessive
than the next woman.</i>

361
00:24:03,475 --> 00:24:05,569
Are you possessive, detective?

362
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:09,248
It wouldn't bother you to know

363
00:24:09,415 --> 00:24:12,351
that Ray Wallace was
sleeping with someone else?

364
00:24:13,118 --> 00:24:14,586
Not at all.

365
00:24:14,753 --> 00:24:18,520
My relationship with Ray
was a purely physical one.

366
00:24:18,691 --> 00:24:22,093
We both wanted
the same thing, sex.

367
00:24:22,828 --> 00:24:25,024
Not love, not marriage,

368
00:24:25,397 --> 00:24:27,525
just sex.

369
00:24:27,766 --> 00:24:31,032
Haven't you ever had a
relationship like that, detective?

370
00:24:31,203 --> 00:24:33,263
Where all you wanted
to do was get into bed?

371
00:24:33,539 --> 00:24:35,599
You didn't answer my question.

372
00:24:38,110 --> 00:24:39,578
The truth,

373
00:24:39,745 --> 00:24:43,113
I encouraged Ray to
seek out other partners.

374
00:24:43,615 --> 00:24:45,516
Practice makes
perfect. Don't you agree?

375
00:24:45,684 --> 00:24:48,381
This free-love attitude
of yours, it's very hip.

376
00:24:48,554 --> 00:24:50,489
You should be on <i>Oprah.</i>

377
00:24:50,923 --> 00:24:52,391
That's all. You can go.

378
00:24:55,694 --> 00:24:57,458
Oh, Miss Perleen.

379
00:24:57,629 --> 00:25:04,160
If you, as you say, encouraged
Ray to, uh, seek out other partners,

380
00:25:04,503 --> 00:25:07,063
why didn't he tell
you about Marsha?

381
00:25:07,373 --> 00:25:09,103
I don't know.

382
00:25:09,274 --> 00:25:11,573
That's a very good question.

383
00:25:12,411 --> 00:25:14,471
Thanks for coming down.

384
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,100
Well, she's some piece of work.

385
00:25:40,272 --> 00:25:41,900
She was toying with you.

386
00:25:42,574 --> 00:25:43,974
Why?

387
00:25:44,543 --> 00:25:47,638
Well, I think this whole
thing's a big game to her.

388
00:25:47,813 --> 00:25:52,251
Yeah? Well, if she killed Ray Wallace,
this is one game she's not gonna win.

389
00:26:01,427 --> 00:26:05,865
I take my wife to physical therapy
every Monday, Wednesday and Friday.

390
00:26:06,031 --> 00:26:07,727
Do you always come
home at the same time?

391
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:11,200
No. Sometimes we go
to the pool afterwards

392
00:26:11,370 --> 00:26:13,362
or to a movie or out to eat.

393
00:26:13,539 --> 00:26:16,270
We get home at
all different times.

394
00:26:16,742 --> 00:26:18,370
Does your car
make a lot of noise?

395
00:26:18,544 --> 00:26:20,570
Heh, it better not.
It's brand-new.

396
00:26:20,746 --> 00:26:22,266
It wouldn't make any
difference anyway.

397
00:26:22,414 --> 00:26:25,145
The stereo was so loud
she couldn't have heard it.

398
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:28,144
All right, thanks,
Mr. Yates. You can go home.

399
00:26:28,320 --> 00:26:29,686
Hmm.

400
00:26:30,055 --> 00:26:31,717
Thank you.

401
00:26:32,491 --> 00:26:34,460
How did she do it?

402
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:40,328
You think her scheme really depended
on, uh, this gentleman seeing her?

403
00:26:40,499 --> 00:26:42,092
Look, she had to have known

404
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:45,635
when he and his wife were
gonna be home that night.

405
00:26:47,306 --> 00:26:49,002
Wait a minute.

406
00:26:49,241 --> 00:26:51,039
Stay there.

407
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:03,479
Get into bed with me.

408
00:27:03,655 --> 00:27:05,123
What?

409
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:07,759
Get into bed. Come on.

410
00:27:09,561 --> 00:27:11,655
- I'll be gentle.
- No.

411
00:27:11,830 --> 00:27:13,510
What, do you think I'm
gonna try something?

412
00:27:13,665 --> 00:27:15,930
Get in the bed.

413
00:27:26,245 --> 00:27:29,374
I don't feel right about this.

414
00:27:32,851 --> 00:27:35,446
You're fabulous in bed.

415
00:27:37,456 --> 00:27:38,651
I'm getting up.

416
00:27:38,824 --> 00:27:40,349
Ah-ah, Come on, come on.

417
00:27:40,526 --> 00:27:43,291
See? That's it.

418
00:27:44,997 --> 00:27:46,295
That's how she knew.

419
00:27:46,465 --> 00:27:49,367
Every time Yates pulls in his
driveway, his lights shine in here.

420
00:27:49,635 --> 00:27:53,094
Yeah, she sees the
light, makes some excuse

421
00:27:53,272 --> 00:27:55,503
and leaves the room.

422
00:27:56,441 --> 00:27:57,534
I'll kill the music.

423
00:27:58,911 --> 00:28:00,391
She comes in, throws
on that disguise,

424
00:28:00,546 --> 00:28:02,146
must've had it stashed
in here somewhere,

425
00:28:02,314 --> 00:28:05,944
goes outside, shoots Ray,
knowing Mr. Yates would see her

426
00:28:06,118 --> 00:28:10,078
and give the police a
description that fits Rick Hamlin.

427
00:28:10,255 --> 00:28:14,215
Then she drops the callous
scraper, comes back inside,

428
00:28:14,393 --> 00:28:16,385
takes off the
disguise, hides it,

429
00:28:16,562 --> 00:28:20,329
and then she pours some wine.

430
00:28:20,499 --> 00:28:22,059
That way, it looks
like she had a reason

431
00:28:22,201 --> 00:28:23,760
to be in here when Ray was shot.

432
00:28:23,936 --> 00:28:26,098
Then it's back to the
bedroom, sees the body,

433
00:28:26,271 --> 00:28:27,591
does that <i>Screaming
Mimi</i> routine.

434
00:28:27,739 --> 00:28:30,174
Mr. Yates comes running
and gives her an alibi.

435
00:28:30,342 --> 00:28:31,582
Then after the police are gone,

436
00:28:31,710 --> 00:28:34,874
she just dumps the cap and
the gun in somebody's trash.

437
00:28:35,113 --> 00:28:36,672
What's up?

438
00:28:36,882 --> 00:28:39,215
- Did I miss something?
- The bottle.

439
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:42,582
If they were having
wine, where's the bottle?

440
00:29:38,577 --> 00:29:40,205
- Morning.
- Morning.

441
00:29:40,379 --> 00:29:41,574
I'm looking for somebody.

442
00:29:41,747 --> 00:29:44,979
- Oh, great.
- A woman, short, late 50s.

443
00:29:45,150 --> 00:29:47,483
She wears a red sweatshirt,
a yellow bandanna.

444
00:29:47,653 --> 00:29:48,780
Good luck, honey.

445
00:29:48,954 --> 00:29:50,388
She was seen Wednesday night

446
00:29:50,555 --> 00:29:54,617
going through the garbage cans
on the 1400 block of Forest Lane.

447
00:29:58,196 --> 00:30:01,997
The man I work for is
real anxious to talk to her.

448
00:30:02,167 --> 00:30:04,295
I know where she is.
Give me the money.

449
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:07,029
Okay! Okay! Wait a second!

450
00:30:07,205 --> 00:30:09,902
There's something about this
woman that I didn't mention.

451
00:30:10,075 --> 00:30:13,307
Something that makes her
immediately recognizable.

452
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:17,245
Whoever can tell me what
that is, gets the money.

453
00:30:17,783 --> 00:30:22,118
She's a... She's got two...
Well, she probably got two heads.

454
00:30:22,287 --> 00:30:23,721
She keeps all her stuff

455
00:30:23,889 --> 00:30:27,018
in a double-decker
shopping cart from Value-Rite.

456
00:30:27,459 --> 00:30:29,451
Bingo. What's her name?

457
00:30:29,628 --> 00:30:31,256
Bea.

458
00:30:31,763 --> 00:30:33,231
I know where she is too.

459
00:30:33,398 --> 00:30:35,196
I know where she isn't.

460
00:30:36,702 --> 00:30:38,068
Ah-ah-ah.

461
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:42,069
- Hey.
- Oh, man.

462
00:30:48,180 --> 00:30:49,648
You sure you know where she is?

463
00:30:49,815 --> 00:30:52,717
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

464
00:30:57,656 --> 00:30:58,680
There.

465
00:31:04,529 --> 00:31:06,191
- Thanks.
- Uh...

466
00:31:06,598 --> 00:31:10,194
Don't tell her I sicced you
on her. She's kind of loony.

467
00:31:10,369 --> 00:31:13,498
Some say she carries a ax.

468
00:31:48,540 --> 00:31:50,133
I'm out here, Mr. Matlock.

469
00:31:56,715 --> 00:31:58,479
Well, you got here just in time.

470
00:31:58,884 --> 00:31:59,908
In time for what?

471
00:32:01,019 --> 00:32:02,544
Come on in.

472
00:32:15,967 --> 00:32:19,096
Would you put some
suntan lotion on my back?

473
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:24,141
Oh, well, I don't know.

474
00:32:26,845 --> 00:32:31,977
They say too much sun
is not good for a person.

475
00:32:32,150 --> 00:32:34,949
I know, but I love the heat.

476
00:32:37,889 --> 00:32:41,417
Go ahead. Spread it all over me.

477
00:32:43,361 --> 00:32:44,385
Mm.

478
00:32:44,563 --> 00:32:47,260
Oh, that feels so good.

479
00:32:47,866 --> 00:32:49,801
Would you spread it
on my legs too, please?

480
00:32:53,605 --> 00:32:54,971
Well...

481
00:32:55,740 --> 00:32:58,801
So tell me, why are you here?

482
00:33:02,447 --> 00:33:06,942
Oh, I wanted to ask you about
that wine you were pouring

483
00:33:07,118 --> 00:33:09,747
when Ray was shot.

484
00:33:11,456 --> 00:33:13,118
Don't stop. Keep doing it.

485
00:33:17,362 --> 00:33:19,354
What'd you do with the bottle?

486
00:33:19,798 --> 00:33:20,822
What do you mean?

487
00:33:20,999 --> 00:33:26,734
There wasn't a half-empty or empty
bottle of red wine in Ray's house,

488
00:33:26,905 --> 00:33:32,674
so I wondered where you got the
wine you spilled in the bedroom from.

489
00:33:33,378 --> 00:33:35,210
Now, where do you
think I got it from?

490
00:33:35,380 --> 00:33:41,377
Well, there was an empty
bottle of, uh, red wine

491
00:33:41,553 --> 00:33:46,514
found outside Ray's
house in the trash can,

492
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:51,720
so maybe you poured those
two glasses earlier in the day

493
00:33:51,897 --> 00:33:53,991
and stashed them away someplace.

494
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:56,935
Now, why would I do
something like that?

495
00:33:57,269 --> 00:33:59,204
Oh, I don't know.

496
00:33:59,371 --> 00:34:04,332
Maybe you realized that
you were pressed for time.

497
00:34:04,509 --> 00:34:08,105
And you had to go
out of the bedroom

498
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:11,614
and dress up like Rick and
run outside and shoot Ray

499
00:34:11,783 --> 00:34:14,878
and run back in the house
and get rid of the costume,

500
00:34:15,053 --> 00:34:20,082
go back in the bedroom,
all in two minutes, no more.

501
00:34:20,258 --> 00:34:21,419
Heh.

502
00:34:21,593 --> 00:34:26,896
Oh, so you think I shot Ray?

503
00:34:31,136 --> 00:34:32,764
Well, you're wrong.

504
00:34:32,938 --> 00:34:34,498
Although, you are
right about one thing.

505
00:34:34,639 --> 00:34:38,542
I did pour the wine earlier that
day while I was fixing dinner.

506
00:34:38,710 --> 00:34:42,613
But then when Ray came
home, we just made love.

507
00:34:43,481 --> 00:34:45,211
Forgot about the wine.

508
00:34:46,217 --> 00:34:47,977
Didn't you ever have
that happen to you, Ben?

509
00:34:48,119 --> 00:34:51,988
Where an overwhelming desire for
sex just made you change your plans?

510
00:34:53,491 --> 00:34:55,824
No, not lately.

511
00:34:56,895 --> 00:34:58,830
That's a shame.

512
00:34:59,731 --> 00:35:01,791
Excuse me.

513
00:35:29,694 --> 00:35:33,290
This one, this one. That's a
good one. What do you think?

514
00:35:34,633 --> 00:35:35,657
What do you think?

515
00:35:37,268 --> 00:35:39,931
Well, hello, sailor.

516
00:35:40,739 --> 00:35:43,538
- Hi.
- Nope. Never saw her.

517
00:35:43,708 --> 00:35:45,233
Maybe she never came in here.

518
00:35:45,410 --> 00:35:47,606
Well, if Ray and
Marsha hung out in here,

519
00:35:47,779 --> 00:35:51,238
it stands to reason that
Sharon would've see them here.

520
00:35:51,416 --> 00:35:54,511
Hey, I recognize those
threads. Where did you get them?

521
00:35:54,686 --> 00:35:56,814
Vintage clothing.

522
00:35:57,589 --> 00:36:00,457
Since you got such a
good memory, ever see her?

523
00:36:00,625 --> 00:36:02,389
Well, I don't notice
girls too much.

524
00:36:02,560 --> 00:36:05,359
So you wanna dance?

525
00:36:05,830 --> 00:36:07,731
- No.
- Do I hear wedding bells?

526
00:36:08,366 --> 00:36:09,664
- Forget it.
- Oh, come on.

527
00:36:09,834 --> 00:36:11,302
- He's a nice boy.
- Forget it.

528
00:36:11,469 --> 00:36:13,370
- Works steady.
- Forget it.

529
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:14,972
All right.

530
00:36:17,375 --> 00:36:20,072
We can't just sit here anymore.
I've gotta do something.

531
00:36:20,245 --> 00:36:24,580
Look, Judy Gale, Tim,
you take care of Ben.

532
00:36:31,589 --> 00:36:33,182
Sorry.

533
00:36:33,391 --> 00:36:34,882
Yeah, okay.

534
00:36:35,060 --> 00:36:36,528
I'm really sorry.

535
00:36:53,078 --> 00:36:56,014
Excuse me. Ahem,
ahem. Excuse me.

536
00:36:56,347 --> 00:36:59,078
Look, could I have
your attention, please?

537
00:36:59,250 --> 00:37:03,483
I... Excuse me, I said, could
I have your attention, please?

538
00:37:03,655 --> 00:37:05,248
Hey.

539
00:37:05,824 --> 00:37:06,848
Hey.

540
00:37:08,159 --> 00:37:10,788
Yeah, could we drop this music?

541
00:37:10,962 --> 00:37:13,454
- Well, that's more like it.
- What's going on?

542
00:37:13,631 --> 00:37:16,430
- Okay, um, uh...
- What's wrong with you?

543
00:37:16,601 --> 00:37:18,729
Most of you know who I am.

544
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:20,462
- No.
- One or two of you do not.

545
00:37:20,839 --> 00:37:22,137
- The lucky ones.
- Ha, ha.

546
00:37:22,307 --> 00:37:24,606
This from a guy that gets
his hair done at Pet World.

547
00:37:27,045 --> 00:37:28,377
Okay.

548
00:37:28,546 --> 00:37:32,278
My name is Lieutenant Pat
Poletti. I'm a police officer.

549
00:37:32,450 --> 00:37:35,716
I'm conducting a murder
investigation, and I would like to know

550
00:37:35,887 --> 00:37:39,824
if any one of you has ever
seen this lovely woman in here?

551
00:37:39,991 --> 00:37:42,586
Here, pass this around,
would you? Go on.

552
00:37:42,761 --> 00:37:45,230
- Pass it back here.
- Okay, pass it around, get a good look

553
00:37:45,396 --> 00:37:47,797
and tell me if anyone has
seen her. Anyone at all.

554
00:37:48,066 --> 00:37:51,764
Come on. Anybody
at all. Get a good look.

555
00:37:51,936 --> 00:37:55,270
Don't be shy. Step right
up. Tell us all about it.

556
00:37:55,440 --> 00:37:58,376
- Anyone?
- No. Sorry.

557
00:37:59,811 --> 00:38:03,612
Well, maybe she wore a
disguise when she came in here.

558
00:38:03,782 --> 00:38:06,980
No, I don't think so, Ben. Let's
face it, this has been a dead end.

559
00:38:07,152 --> 00:38:09,519
But at least you had fun
with Tim and Judy Gale.

560
00:38:09,687 --> 00:38:11,155
Oh, changed my life.

561
00:38:11,322 --> 00:38:12,756
Well, I won't tell anyone.

562
00:38:12,924 --> 00:38:14,688
- Ticket?
- Yup.

563
00:38:18,696 --> 00:38:21,962
Do you always write down the
license-plate number on these?

564
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:23,362
Sure do.

565
00:38:23,535 --> 00:38:25,367
- Do you keep them?
- Yeah.

566
00:38:25,537 --> 00:38:28,097
- How long?
- Ah, a few months.

567
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:42,678
Did you ever go to a
nightclub called Martell's?

568
00:38:42,854 --> 00:38:43,878
No.

569
00:38:44,055 --> 00:38:46,388
- Are you sure?
- I'm positive.

570
00:38:47,192 --> 00:38:52,995
Is the license-plate number
on your car LSP3A7?

571
00:38:53,164 --> 00:38:54,188
Yes, it is.

572
00:38:55,033 --> 00:39:00,631
Um, this parking stub
was taken, with a warrant,

573
00:39:00,805 --> 00:39:05,038
from the attendant
at Martell's yesterday.

574
00:39:05,210 --> 00:39:10,376
The attendants there, uh, mark down
the license-plate number on the ticket

575
00:39:10,548 --> 00:39:12,176
for every car they park,

576
00:39:12,350 --> 00:39:13,841
and they keep them
up to six months.

577
00:39:14,018 --> 00:39:15,543
Something to do with insurance.

578
00:39:15,720 --> 00:39:19,248
Would you just read the
license-plate number on this ticket?

579
00:39:21,392 --> 00:39:24,726
"LSP3A7."

580
00:39:25,029 --> 00:39:28,193
That's your
license-plate number.

581
00:39:28,633 --> 00:39:30,397
Yes, it is.

582
00:39:30,568 --> 00:39:32,408
I guess the attendant
must have made a mistake.

583
00:39:33,771 --> 00:39:36,297
Or it could be
that you're lying.

584
00:39:36,474 --> 00:39:39,069
It could be that you
did go to Martell's,

585
00:39:39,244 --> 00:39:43,204
and that you did see your boyfriend,
Ray Wallace, with Marsha Dunn there.

586
00:39:43,982 --> 00:39:49,649
And either right then or sometime
soon thereafter, you what,

587
00:39:49,821 --> 00:39:51,756
decided to kill them both?

588
00:39:53,625 --> 00:39:56,595
I'm sorry, Mr. Matlock, is
there a date on that stub?

589
00:39:56,761 --> 00:39:59,356
Yes. "May 29th."

590
00:39:59,530 --> 00:40:01,396
That explains it.

591
00:40:01,566 --> 00:40:03,797
Well, my sister was in
town and I lent her my car

592
00:40:03,968 --> 00:40:06,096
and she must have
gone to Martell's.

593
00:40:06,271 --> 00:40:08,831
She doesn't get a chance to go
to nightclubs very much, you know.

594
00:40:08,973 --> 00:40:11,306
She lives in Mason City, Iowa.

595
00:40:22,887 --> 00:40:24,150
Mr. Matlock?

596
00:40:25,023 --> 00:40:28,255
Oh, I have no more
questions, Your Honor.

597
00:40:28,526 --> 00:40:30,154
The witness may step down.

598
00:40:31,129 --> 00:40:36,864
Uh, Your Honor, uh, I have
one more witness I'd like to call,

599
00:40:37,035 --> 00:40:41,029
but with the court's permission,
I'd like to wait till in the morning.

600
00:40:41,439 --> 00:40:43,601
Sounds like a good
idea to me, Mr. Matlock.

601
00:40:44,409 --> 00:40:48,210
Court will reconvene
at 9 a.m. tomorrow.

602
00:42:53,104 --> 00:42:56,802
Why, Grandma, what
a big knife you have.

603
00:43:11,522 --> 00:43:13,991
A little help here, please.

604
00:43:14,158 --> 00:43:15,786
Guys?

605
00:43:17,395 --> 00:43:19,330
Guys?

606
00:43:21,632 --> 00:43:23,100
Hey.

607
00:43:23,868 --> 00:43:26,303
Hey, a little help
here, guys. Whoa!

608
00:43:26,971 --> 00:43:29,634
Now would be a good time.

609
00:43:31,976 --> 00:43:33,877
Hold it! Police!

610
00:43:35,346 --> 00:43:36,939
- We got her.
- You all right?

611
00:43:37,415 --> 00:43:40,852
Yeah. Thank God for
modern inventions, huh?

612
00:43:41,018 --> 00:43:42,145
Oh.

613
00:43:42,487 --> 00:43:45,013
Well, Miss Perleen,
looks like we got you.

614
00:43:46,624 --> 00:43:48,092
Let's take her to the car.

615
00:43:48,259 --> 00:43:50,459
You have the right to remain
silent. Anything you say...

616
00:43:50,595 --> 00:43:52,689
Yeah.

617
00:43:53,664 --> 00:43:56,463
And some more for
our own prison boy.

618
00:43:56,634 --> 00:43:57,897
- Eat. Eat.
- Oh.

619
00:43:58,069 --> 00:44:01,506
It's awfully good
and great to be free.

620
00:44:01,672 --> 00:44:02,696
Uh-huh.

621
00:44:03,207 --> 00:44:05,802
Unemployed, but free.

622
00:44:05,977 --> 00:44:07,468
Eat. Makes your hair grow.

623
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:09,341
- I never heard that.
- Guaranteed.

624
00:44:09,514 --> 00:44:12,040
My husband, rest his
soul, passed away at 83,

625
00:44:12,216 --> 00:44:14,208
ate pasta every day.

626
00:44:14,385 --> 00:44:15,910
Died, had all his hair.

627
00:44:16,087 --> 00:44:19,080
Yeah, he had also
arthritis, high blood pressure,

628
00:44:19,257 --> 00:44:21,158
high cholesterol and bad feet.

629
00:44:21,325 --> 00:44:24,056
He had his hair.

630
00:44:24,862 --> 00:44:25,921
Oh.

631
00:44:26,764 --> 00:44:28,960
So you bring this
homeless woman into court.

632
00:44:29,133 --> 00:44:30,260
What's her name? Bea?

633
00:44:30,434 --> 00:44:31,458
- Bea.
- Bea.

634
00:44:31,636 --> 00:44:34,470
And this Sharon dame, she
thinks that Bea saw something

635
00:44:34,639 --> 00:44:36,437
and was gonna
testify against her.

636
00:44:36,607 --> 00:44:38,303
- Right? Aha.
- Yeah, yeah.

637
00:44:38,809 --> 00:44:40,607
But what a plan.

638
00:44:40,778 --> 00:44:44,146
You make this Perleen dame
think that my Pat is the bag lady.

639
00:44:44,315 --> 00:44:47,342
Ma, could I please
have some pasta?

640
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:50,716
Why? You looked enough
like the bag lady to be her.

641
00:44:51,389 --> 00:44:52,857
What a plan.

642
00:44:53,024 --> 00:44:55,050
Well, it was your daughter's
plan, it wasn't mine.

643
00:44:55,226 --> 00:44:58,526
- Oh, thank you.
- Oh, hey, don't get me wrong.

644
00:44:58,696 --> 00:45:03,225
I love my daughter. I
do. More than life itself.

645
00:45:03,401 --> 00:45:06,428
- Ma.
- Let's have a toast.

646
00:45:08,773 --> 00:45:13,211
To Pat and Sophia and Ben

647
00:45:13,778 --> 00:45:17,806
and freedom and pasta and hair.

648
00:45:17,982 --> 00:45:19,712
- Ha, ha. Cin-cin.
- Salute.

649
00:45:20,918 --> 00:45:21,942
- Cin-cin.
- There you go.

650
00:45:22,119 --> 00:45:24,020
Oh, no, you don't.

651
00:45:24,789 --> 00:45:29,250
Oh, Benny, now look
what you've done, huh?

